 * (_mirrorRailGeometry): the chatpane container query cannot reach this
 * subtree, and cannot be extended to it — container-type's layout
 * containment would re-parent the mobile bottom-sheet dropdowns'
 * position:fixed from the viewport to this band. Zero-grant defaults
 * degrade to the no-rail geometry, i.e. exactly the old centering.
 *
 * Width: 52px + --toolbar-w (avatar track + reading track) so BOTH edges
 * align; the middle term keeps the composer on the reading track
 * (min(52 + measure, pane − 48 − furniture)) even when --toolbar-w's floor
 * shrinks; the outer min(…, 100% − 48px) is the viewport cap (a genuinely
 * fat toolbar may still outgrow the track — it grows RIGHT, into the empty
 * rail zone, never past the viewport). --toolbar-w is a RESOLVED pixel
 * value written by main.js from the toolbar's natural width at
 * max-width:9999px — blind to the rail furniture, so with the adaptive
 * rail (2026-09-24) the fat-toolbar term can outgrow the text column and
 * let the composer extend into the rail zone — the documented fat-toolbar
 * escape, not a desync: the geometry sweep's composer formula was updated
 * to the furniture-aware cap for exactly this.
 * .input-area carries NO horizontal padding so 100% here IS the pane width.
 *
 * min-width:300px is the HOPELESS-PANE floor: with the inspector drawer
 * open beside a wide sidebar the pane can drop below 100px, where the
 * track math would squeeze the composer to a useless sliver (and the
 * status strip's gauge/dots would spill out of it). The floor keeps the
 * textarea usable; the right side simply continues under the fixed
 * drawer — exactly what the whole composer did before the margin-right,
 * now bounded to one small overrun. Mobile (≤768px) resets it to 0 — the
 * drawer is a full-width overlay there and every px counts.
